pySMESH: make StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D with viscous layers stop on a cancel (SMESH V9_16_0).

Symptom: with a ViscousLayers hypothesis, a cancel (SMESH_Gen::CancelCompute, or a progress
hook that cancels) that arrives while the offset shape is built is lost: the grid step and
the layer step run to their end, and the compute reports the cancel only after the complete
mesh is built. A cancel during the layer step is not seen before the step ends either.

Upstream commits: the viscous layers path of StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D::Compute and
StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL came with SMESH c9294ee68 (2022-06-17, bos #17015, "Body fitting
with Viscous Layers for CFD meshing") and was reworked by d3c3260cd (2023-07-25, bos #35147,
"Decompose Viscous Layer API"). Upstream master at 83f8bf482 (2026-09-14) has the same code.

Root cause: with a ViscousLayers hypothesis, Compute builds the offset shape
(ViscousBuilder::MakeOffsetShape), then calls itself on it. The inner call resets the member
flag _computeCanceled at its start, as Compute without viscous layers does, so a cancel that
came during the offset step is cleared before the grid step can read it. The layer step,
ViscousBuilder::MakeViscousLayers, has no access to the flag and no check.

Change (the cancel path only; a run without a cancel builds the same mesh):
* StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D.cxx, StdMeshers_Cartesian_3D::Compute: return false when the flag
  is set after the offset step; the inner call (_isComputeOffset) does not reset the flag,
  which was reset before the outer call (SMESH_Algo::InitComputeError); pass the flag to
  MakeViscousLayers.
* StdMeshers_Cartesian_VL.hxx and .cxx, ViscousBuilder::MakeViscousLayers: a new last
  parameter, volatile bool* theComputeCanceled (default 0, so that the other caller,
  StdMeshers_ViscousLayerBuilder::AddLayers, is unchanged). The flag is read at the phase
  boundaries: before the main mesh is cleared, after each shape type of the projection
  loop, after the prisms, before and after the offset mesh is copied to the main one, after
  the boundary elements are set to sub-meshes, and after the coincident nodes are merged.
  When it is set, the function returns false and builds nothing more.

Not changed: ViscousBuilder::MakeOffsetShape is one OCCT offset (BRepOffset_MakeOffset) and
cannot be stopped inside; the cancel is read when it returns. copyMesh() and the node merge
(SMESH_MeshEditor) have no check inside; the latency is bounded by the longest of these
phases.

